# Per-machine credentials for this repo's pipeline agents (spec 013).
#
# The pipeline agents consume exactly two GitHub credentials per machine. This
# template enumerates those two — nothing invented. ONE-TIME SETUP (direnv):
#   1. Copy this file to config/agent.local.env and fill in real values:
#        cp config/agent.local.env.example config/agent.local.env
#   2. The repo-root .envrc (a gitignored copy of templates/.envrc.example)
#      loads this file via its third dotenv_if_exists line when you run
#      `direnv allow` at the repo root — no manual sourcing needed.
#   3. NEVER commit config/agent.local.env — scripts/guard-env.sh and the
#      .gitignore rule make that structural (self-ci enforces both).

# GITHUB_TOKEN — personal access token for the GitHub MCP server
# (okf/mcp-server-connection.md) and PR diagnostic comments (docs/TESTING.md).
# Create a fine-grained PAT with repo scope at
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens.
GITHUB_TOKEN=<your-github-personal-access-token>

# GH_TOKEN — gh CLI / release-automation credential (docs/CI_CD.md §Release
# Process); the spec PR Opener uses it to push the spec branch and open the
# draft PR. Reuse the fine-grained token above scoped to this repo only
# (spec 026, AC-026-12): a classic PAT carries org-wide blast radius on a
# developer machine that also feeds an autonomous pipeline agent — prefer
# it only if a fine-grained PAT genuinely cannot cover a required scope
# (e.g. an org-level API this repo's scripts do not otherwise need).
GH_TOKEN=<your-github-personal-access-token>

# JUDGMENT_API_KEY — bearer credential for the opt-in typed-judgment layer
# (spec 028, scripts/typed-judgment.sh). Commented out by default: with it
# unset, typed-judgment.sh exits 10 and every consumer runs its stock
# procedure unchanged. When you opt in, put the real value only in your
# gitignored config/agent.local.env — never here.
# This key is REQUIRED only for hosted backends; it is optional when
# JUDGMENT_BACKEND=local — local backends may not require authentication,
# and the request is then sent without any Authorization header (spec 029,
# ADR 0005). Set it only if you configured your local server with a key.
# JUDGMENT_API_KEY=<your-judgment-api-key>
